{% extends "lab-base.html.j2" %}
{% block title %}Research & contributions{% endblock %}
{% block content %}
<header class="lab-header"><p class="eyebrow">Open science / A contribution you can inspect</p><h1>Real data.<br><span class="title-muted">Useful, checkable work.</span></h1><p class="lead">Theoxenia independently processes public scientific recordings. Our contribution is the reproducible analysis: inputs, methods, checks, limitations and compact results.</p></header>
<div class="callout-note"><strong>Current status: recorded analyses, no external acceptance claimed.</strong><p>The telescope recordings are real. The recovery controls are synthetic and labelled separately. Report 01 is published on Zenodo with its source snapshot and evidence. No scientific-team acceptance or external peer review is claimed.</p></div>
{% if report %}
<section class="section-block report-feature" id="first-report">
<p class="eyebrow">Research report 01 / Real archive data / 18 October 2026</p>
<h2>Empty tables.<br><span class="title-muted">Tested boundaries.</span></h2>
<p class="lead">An empty table deserves an explanation. We replayed six telescope scans, checked the detector with independent calculations, and planted known signals in the measured backgrounds.</p>
<div class="research-grid"><article class="check-card"><p class="eyebrow">01 / Reproduce</p><h3>Four empty scans, explained</h3><p>Both calculations stay below the search threshold. The corrected detector recovers all 20 artificial controls in those four scans.</p></article><article class="check-card"><p class="eyebrow">02 / Correct</p><h3>A wider, verified search</h3><p>A drift-coverage fix extends the tested boundary from ±3.827 to ±3.990 Hz/s. It adds one measured OFF-scan hit.</p></article><article class="check-card"><p class="eyebrow">03 / Keep the limits</p><h3>24 of 30 controls retained</h3><p>Six controls are lost during stronger-neighbor selection in crowded scans. This is a measured detector limit, not survey completeness.</p></article></div>
<figure class="report-figure"><img src="reports/first-results/diagnosis-overview.svg" alt="Six-scan comparison: maximum scores in scans three to six remain below ten; corrected five-track recovery is one, three, five, five, five and five."><figcaption class="figure-note">Left: maximum normalized score, logarithmic scale. Right: matching top hits on identical five-track injected copies. Artificial controls are separate from the original observations. <a href="reports/first-results/diagnosis-overview.svg">Open full-size figure →</a></figcaption></figure>
<div class="table-scroll"><table class="hit-table"><caption>Corrected per-scan results · one 1380–1381 MHz cadence</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Scan</th><th scope="col">Pointing</th><th scope="col">Top hits</th><th scope="col">Detector max</th><th scope="col">Independent max</th><th scope="col">Controls</th></tr></thead><tbody>{% for row in report.rows %}<tr><th scope="row">{{ row.scan }} · {{ row.role }}</th><td>{{ row.source }}</td><td>{{ row.hits }}</td><td>{{ '%.3f'|format(row.turboseti_max) }}</td><td>{{ '%.3f'|format(row.independent_max) }}</td><td>{{ row.controls_recovered }} / {{ row.controls_injected }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}</tbody></table></div>
<div class="report-actions"><a class="button-link" href="reports/first-results/report.pdf">Read the five-page report ↓</a><a class="button-link secondary" href="downloads/research-report-evidence.zip">Download the evidence ↓</a><a href="reports/first-results/README.md">Reproduction instructions</a></div>
<p class="figure-note">Published on Zenodo · <a href="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23489303">DOI 10.5281/zenodo.23489303</a> · No external peer review. The original 273-row explorer is preserved; the corrected 336 per-scan hits are not a new clustered cadence table. <a href="reports/first-results/SUBMISSION.md">Publication routes and metadata review</a>.</p>
</section>
{% endif %}
<section class="section-block"><h2>Where this work can go</h2><div class="research-grid">
<article class="check-card"><p class="eyebrow">01 / Preserve &amp; cite</p><h3>Zenodo research record</h3><p>Publish a versioned analysis report, code snapshot and processed tables. Zenodo registers a DOI when a record is published. A DOI makes the work citable; it does not mean the scientific conclusion has passed peer review.</p><a href="https://help.zenodo.org/docs/deposit/about-records/">Zenodo record guidance ↗</a><p class="figure-note">Report 01 published 20 October 2026 · <a href="https://zenodo.org/records/23489303">Open the research record ↗</a>.</p></article>
<article class="check-card"><p class="eyebrow">02 / Contribute to the tools</p><h3>Breakthrough Listen software</h3><p>Berkeley invites work on software and algorithms for its open data. A reproducible defect report, benchmark or tested patch can be useful even when an observation yields no surviving lines. Check each repository's current contribution rules.</p><a href="https://seti.berkeley.edu/listen/data.html">Official open-data participation guide ↗</a><p class="figure-note">No affiliation or endorsement is implied.</p></article>
<article class="check-card"><p class="eyebrow">03 / Discuss a substantial result</p><h3>Scientific collaboration</h3><p>Berkeley publishes a scientific-collaboration contact. Prepare a concise report with the exact observations, processing, checks and unresolved issues before approaching the team. This is a contact route, not an automatic validation service.</p><a href="https://seti.berkeley.edu/contact.html">Official collaboration contact ↗</a><p class="figure-note">No outreach or submission has been made.</p></article>
</div></section>
<section class="section-block"><h2>What makes a useful contribution</h2><div class="method-steps"><p><strong>A bounded question</strong>State the observation, frequency window and method. Report the limits alongside the result.</p><p><strong>A reproducible package</strong>Include the source identifiers, processing version, parameters, checksums and machine-readable results.</p><p><strong>An honest status</strong>Keep processing, internal review, external submission and external acceptance distinct. Link the actual record when a status changes.</p></div></section>
<section class="contribute-panel"><div><p class="eyebrow">Start small</p><h2>Reproduce a result. Improve a check.</h2><p>Use a dossier to retrace the work, then share a concrete discrepancy or improvement through the project repository. Rerunning the historical recovery grid with the corrected detector and testing more cadences are useful next contributions.</p></div><a class="button-link" href="https://github.com/mpetyx/theoxenia/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md">Contributor guide ↗</a></section>
<p class="figure-note">Official destination guidance checked 18 October 2026. Participation pages may describe older programmes; verify the current route before sending work.</p>
